WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.048
Searching a word list means checking every word from its first letter.

00:07.048 --> 00:14.700
When thousands of words share beginnings, all that repeated reading adds up.

00:15.000 --> 00:20.803
A trie stores each shared beginning once.

00:20.803 --> 00:31.700
“apple” and “app” walk the same a-p-p path and branch only where they differ.

00:32.000 --> 00:41.077
Inserting reuses every node already there, then marks where the word ends.

00:41.077 --> 00:47.700
Looking up “app” walks the same path letter by letter.

00:48.000 --> 00:56.681
Each operation costs one hop per letter: O(L).

00:56.681 --> 00:59.700
That’s the trie.

